{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ופרעה הקריב", :translit "u-far'oh hikriv", :gloss "and Pharaoh drew near"} {:he "ופרעה חולם", :translit "u-far'oh holeim", :gloss "and Pharaoh dreamed"} {:he "כאשר כבדו אתכם מצרים ופרעה וגו'", :translit "ka'asher khivdu et'khem mitsrayim u-far'oh ve-gomer", :gloss "just as Egypt burdened you and Pharaoh etc."} {:he "הלא כאשר התעולל בהם", :translit "ha-lo ka'asher hit'olel ba-hem", :gloss "is it not as he toyed with them"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ופרעה הקריב" "ופרעה חולם" "כאשר כבדו אתכם מצרים ופרעה"]}], :frame {:text "Pharaoh dreamed two dreams and Joseph interpreted them (Genesis 41:1–36). After interpretation Joseph asked to be remembered when things went well (Genesis 41:14). Yet the chief butler did not remember Joseph and forgot him (Genesis 41:23). The phrase הלא כאשר התעולל בהם appears at Exodus 10:2.", :sources ["Genesis 41:1–36" "Genesis 41:14" "Genesis 41:23" "Exodus 10:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הקריב", :translit "hikriv", :gloss "drew near / brought near"} {:he "ופרעה הקריב", :translit "u-far'oh hikriv", :gloss "and Pharaoh drew near"} {:he "הקריב את קרבנו", :translit "hikriv et korbano", :gloss "he brought near his sacrifice"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ופרעה הקריב" "הקריב את קרבנו"]}], :frame {:text "Israel encamped before Ba'al Zefon at Exodus 14:2. The mode of writing of הקריב in both occurrences links Pharaoh's drawing near for war with his bringing a sacrifice.", :sources ["Exodus 14:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והנה מצרים נוסע אחריהם", :translit "ve-hineh mitsrayim nosei'a akhareihem", :gloss "and behold Egypt journeying after them"} {:he "עזי וזמרת יה", :translit "uzzi ve-zimrat yah", :gloss "my strength and song of Yah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Reading מצרים as the angelic prince עוזא rather than the nation"}], :frame {:text "Each nation has a celestial prince or patron angel; the prince of Egypt is called עוזא in rabbinic sources (Shemot Rabbah 21:5). The Song of the Sea opens with עזי וזמרת יה at Exodus 15:2. The phrase עזי 'Uzza' is read as an allusion to the prince עוזא.", :sources ["Shemot Rabbah 21:5" "Exodus 15:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ופרעה הקריב" "ופרעה חולם" "כאשר כבדו אתכם מצרים ופרעה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ופרעה הקריב", :refs ["Exodus 14:10"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ופרעה חולם", :refs ["Genesis 41:1" "Genesis 41:25"], :n 2, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "כאשר כבדו אתכם מצרים ופרעה", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ופרעה הקריב" "הקריב את קרבנו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ופרעה הקריב", :refs ["Exodus 14:10"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "הקריב את קרבנו", :refs ["Numbers 6:14" "Numbers 7:19" "Numbers 9:7"], :n 3, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Reading מצרים as the angelic prince עוזא rather than the nation", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:55.597201049Z", :model "glm-5.2"}